Restore `WorkerService.init` on the custom-element stand-in.

Applied to `vendored/ocaml-model-explorer/model-explorer` by `make
visualizer.build`, against `model-explorer-v0.1.32-25-g2a89bd7`. Without it
`ng build custom_element` does not compile and there is no bundle to ship.

WHY THIS IS NEEDED

`src/ui/angular.json` builds the `custom_element` target with a
`fileReplacements` entry that swaps the real worker service for a stand-in:

    components/visualizer/worker_service.ts -> custom_element/worker_service.ts

The stand-in exists so the element takes its worker URL from
`window.modelExplorer.workerScriptPath` instead of an `import.meta.url`
relative path -- which is exactly what lets the bundle be served from a path
prefix, as `web/app/index.html` and the Pages deployment both do.

On 2026-04-06 (`49aa6a8`, "Refactor how worker is initialized") the real
service moved worker construction out of its constructor into
`init(onPortal)`, and `app_service.ts:1114` now calls it. The stand-in has not
been touched since 2025-02-19, so it carries no `init` and the build fails:

    TS2339: Property 'init' does not exist on type 'WorkerService'.
      src/components/visualizer/app_service.ts:1114:23

Nothing upstream catches this. `.github/workflows/build_ui_code.yaml` runs
`npm run build`, which is `ng build model_explorer` only; the `custom_element`
target is built solely by `scripts/build_npm.sh` at release time. That is also
the most likely reason `ai-edge-model-explorer-visualizer` has been stuck at
0.1.2 (2025-06-23) for over a year while `src/ui/src` kept moving.

WHAT IT CHANGES

Only the stand-in, and only to match the interface its consumer now expects:
`init` (re)creates the worker from `workerScriptPath`, preserving the
path-prefix behaviour the stand-in exists for, and `ngOnDestroy` terminates it.
This mirrors the real service's shape without adopting its `import.meta.url`
worker path.

MAINTENANCE

`make visualizer.patch` refuses to build if this no longer applies rather than
skipping it, because a silently unpatched tree fails later and less legibly.
When the submodule is bumped, either re-derive this against the new stand-in or
drop it if upstream has fixed the target. The check that it is still needed is
simply whether `ng build custom_element` succeeds without it.

diff --git a/src/ui/src/custom_element/worker_service.ts b/src/ui/src/custom_element/worker_service.ts
index 93d8d36..10d9cda 100644
--- a/src/ui/src/custom_element/worker_service.ts
+++ b/src/ui/src/custom_element/worker_service.ts
@@ -16,19 +16,26 @@
  * ==============================================================================
  */

-import {Injectable} from '@angular/core';
+import {Injectable, OnDestroy} from '@angular/core';

 /**
  * Service to manage web worker.
  */
 @Injectable()
-export class WorkerService {
-  readonly worker: Worker;
+export class WorkerService implements OnDestroy {
+  worker!: Worker;

-  constructor() {
+  init(onPortal: boolean) {
+    if (this.worker) {
+      this.worker.terminate();
+    }
     const workerScriptUrl =
       // tslint:disable-next-line:no-any
       (window as any)['modelExplorer'].workerScriptPath ?? 'worker.js';
     this.worker = new Worker(workerScriptUrl);
   }
+
+  ngOnDestroy() {
+    this.worker?.terminate();
+  }
 }
